      en: "The Pakaraima Mountains stretch 800 km across Guyana, Venezuela, and Brazil. They are ancient sandstone plateaus, over 1.8 billion years old. Mount Roraima (2,810 m) is the highest. The range contains Kaieteur Falls and many other tepuis. It is a major source of gold and diamonds. The indigenous Pemon people inhabit the region. Annual rainfall averages 3,000 mm.",
